POLYNOMIALS README
------------------

This file describes the different polynomial implementations present in the
utils/ directory.

GENERAL DESCRIPTION
-------------------
There are currently five families of files: cado_poly, double_poly,
modul_poly (in utils/arith/), mpz_poly, and polynomial.hpp.

The cado_poly library implements operations on cado_poly structs, which 
function is to stock the polynomials used for sieving, together with the
number n and the skewness.
 
The double_poly library (formerly fpoly) implements polynomials with
floating-point coefficients, including root refining by dichotomy.
 
The modul_poly files implement arithmetic on modular polynomials, with 
coefficients of the types of the (old) arithmetic layer in utils/arith/.

The mpz_poly files implement polynomials with gmp integers as
coefficients.

polynomial.hpp defines a C++ class template for polynomials over
arbitrary types (a priori float, double, and long double).

